  "question": {
    "text": "The ratio of the nuclear radius, of an atom with mass number <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math> <mrow> <msubsup> <mspace></mspace> <mn>2</mn> <mn>4</mn> </msubsup> <mtext>He&#160;</mtext> </mrow> </math>is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mfenced><mn>14</mn></mfenced><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac></msup></math>. What is the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "56",
  "solution": {
    "text": "From the relation <math> <mrow> <mtext>r</mtext> <mo>&prop;</mo> <msup> <mtext>A</mtext> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>/</mo> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </msup> <mtext>,</mtext> </mrow> </math><br /><br />we have,&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>r</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>r</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>A</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>A</mtext> <mn>1</mn> </msub> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>/</mo> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />or&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <math> <mrow> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mfrac> <mrow> <msub> <mtext>A</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfrac> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>/</mo> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </msup> <mo>=</mo> <msup> <mrow> <mfenced close=\")\" open=\"(\" separators=\",\"> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mn>4</mn> </mrow> </mfenced> </mrow> <mrow> <mn>1</mn> <mo>/</mo> <mn>3</mn> </mrow> </msup> </mrow> </math><br /><br />Therefore, A<sub>2</sub> = 56"
  }
